  "lines": [
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Mia, how do bees make honey?",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "🐝",
          "label": "Bee"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "🍯",
          "label": "Honey?"
        },
        "mid": "?"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "It all starts with flowers! Bees sip a sweet juice from flowers, called nectar.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🌸",
        "text": "Flower nectar",
        "cue": "nectar",
        "sub": "A sweet flower juice",
        "sub_cue": "sweet"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Do they drink it all up?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Not all of it. A bee keeps the nectar in a special honey tummy, and flies it home to the hive.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🐝",
        "text": "A special honey tummy",
        "cue": "tummy",
        "sub": "Then home to the hive",
        "sub_cue": "hive"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "And then it turns into honey?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Almost! At the hive, bees pass the nectar from bee to bee. They mix in special juices, then put it in little wax cells.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "Back at the hive",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🐝",
            "label": "Pass it bee to bee",
            "cue": "pass"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🧪",
            "label": "Mix in bee juices",
            "cue": "mix"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🍯",
            "label": "Into little wax cells",
            "cue": "cells"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "But nectar is runny. Honey is thick!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Great noticing! The bees fan their wings super fast to dry out the water. That makes it thick and sticky.",
      "punch": "fan",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🌬️",
        "text": "Fanning wings dry it out",
        "cue": "fan",
        "sub": "Thick and sticky!",
        "sub_cue": "thick"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "When it's ready, they close each little cell with a wax lid, like a tiny jar.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🍯",
        "text": "Sealed with a wax lid",
        "cue": "wax",
        "sub": "Like a tiny jar!",
        "sub_cue": "jar"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Why do bees save so much honey?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "It's their food for winter, when there are no flowers. And honey can keep for a very long time!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "❄️",
        "text": "Food for winter",
        "cue": "winter",
        "sub": "Honey keeps a long time",
        "sub_cue": "keep"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So they sip nectar, pass it around, fan it dry, and seal it up. Honey!",
      "board": {
        "type": "summary",
        "rows": [
          {
            "icon": "🌸",
            "text": "Sip nectar",
            "cue": "sip"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🐝",
            "text": "Pass it around",
            "cue": "pass"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🌬️",
            "text": "Fan it dry",
            "cue": "fan"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🍯",
            "text": "Seal it up",
            "cue": "seal"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Sweet job! Ask a grown-up to subscribe to The Curio Kids Club for more wonders! And next time someone asks... how do bees make honey?"
